ority.\n2|\n3|Verify with your own instruments: (1) Section 2.4 fixtures — for each of the seven normative fixtures (PROFILE-DIRECT-TAKEOVER/RESUME/FORK, PROFILE-TB-TAKEOVER/RESUME/FORK, PROFILE-PI-EQUAL-MAPPING) reconstruct the P0/E1/C1 scenario yourself through the production entries (Derive/DeriveForHeads, BundlePair, ForkProjection, FinalizePair, Check* pairs) over a real sessrepo chain and assert the exact required authority pairs (P1/E1, P1/null, source_profile_event_id=E1); confirm a losing-lease profile.changed and an ambiguous event never change the effective profile, that a closure containing E1 never falls back to P0, and that P0-after-C1, missing E1 and an inconsistent bundle profile refuse integrity_failure. (2) SetProfile transaction — drive Transactor.SetProfile: happy path appends exactly one profile.changed under the current lease; from == to refused; yolo without confirmation refused; stale epoch, divergent token and greater-epoch acting lease refused; retry with the identical request envelope replays the committed event without a second append (assert the chain length and bytes); a retry with a changed envelope member is refused or appends a distinct event — state which and why per the pinned text; crash injection between mint and append leaves no partial event admitted (rerun the producer's crash_test twice and add your own seam). (3) Section 7.7 mapping — extract the table yourself and diff against provhost.ResolveMapping/ProjectLaunchArgv: exact flags for Codex/Claude/Gemini/Muse/Antigravity, Pi 0.73.1 default_unrestricted_tool_set report-only with the equivalence disclosed, the codex `--yolo` alias refused for persistence, standard emitting no unrestricted flag and refusing a machine-local alias, exact-version probe required before mapping, an absent or changed flag failing closed, profile_mapping_unavailable exit 6 with provider/version/profile details registered through internal/axerror (confirm it is a legitimate registered class and no oth