{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c675","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ae11-04bd-7bb0-aac5-3ecca198188f"},"sequence":405,"recorded_at":1780531400000805,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"a44b1373-1c97-4578-936f-97327477c22e","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"a44b1373-1c97-4578-936f-97327477c22e","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"a44b1373-1c97-4578-936f-97327477c22e"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0ae11-f5d0-7050-a47c-11f2a9b1d4a3"},"task_id":"01a0ae11-f5d0-7050-a47c-11f2a9b1d4a3","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0ae11-f5d0-7050-a47c-11f2a9b1d4a3","chunk":"Read text file `internal/sessprofile/doc.go`.\n1|// Package sessprofile derives and persists the Section 2.4 effective\n2|// execution profile: the Session Record creation value followed by the\n3|// newest authoritative profile.changed event in lease/sequence order.\n4|//\n5|// Normative scope: AX v0.6.0 Sections 2.4 (execution profiles, the\n6|// seven PROFILE-* fixtures), 5.1/5.2 (the creation member and the\n7|// launch/resume/fork/profile.changed payload pairs), 5.4 (the\n8|// checkpoint event-head closure that fixes the pair), 7.7 (the\n9|// provider mapping the launch projection resolves — owned by\n10|// internal/provhost), and 9.3 (the Task-board Bundle pair). Sections\n11|// 2.4 and 7.7 are textually identical in v0.5.0. Sections 5.5 and 8\n12|// are the tuple authority behind the mapping resolver, not profile\n13|// authority: provider mapping strings are evidence, never the\n14|// persisted profile.\n15|//\n16|// Division of authority inside this story:\n17|//\n18|//   - Durable session state — the immutable record, the ordered event\n19|//     chain, sequence continuity, and attestation — is owned by\n20|//     internal/sessrepo and reached only through its production\n21|//     entries. Decode projects members from attested bytes and never\n22|//     re-verifies; MintChangeEvent computes the omit-self digest of\n23|//     bytes it authors through canonicaljson.CalculateObjectIdentity\n24|//     (the CreateIdentity precedent) and never calls\n25|//     VerifyObjectIdentity, so the provhost\n26|//     no-attestation-outside-the-leaf bound holds: only the sessrepo\n27|//     append path attests the minted event.\n28|//   - Lifecycle derivation stays with internal/sessstate, which\n29|//     treats profile.changed and the profile pairs as inert facts.\n30|//     This package derives the profile pair only and re-checks chain\n31|//     continuity over its input for the same reason sessstate does:\n32|//     a chain-forbidden reordering refuses instead of silently\n33|//     deriving a different pair.\n34|//   - Lease/authority admission stays with sessrepo (chain order) and\n35|//     internal/sessquery (the winning-lease checkpoint admission,\n36|//     whose checkCheckpointProfileAuthority is the admission twin of\n37|//     DeriveForHeads). That twin's closure capability is unexported\n38|//     and bound to the selector Reader, so no external package can\n39|//     consume it; this package therefore defines its closure input\n40|//     explicitly — heads over the sessrepo chain index, transitive\n41|//     predecessors, the Session Record digest as the genesis\n42|//     terminal, index membership as authority — with identical\n43|//     closure semantics.\n44|//   - The Section 7.7 mapping table and the exact-version probe gate\n45|//     stay with internal/provhost (ProfileMapping, CheckResumeTuple,\n46|//     ResolveMapping). This package never maps a profile to a flag.\n47|//   - Takeover, resume, fork, materialization, and bridge\n48|//     transactions stay with their owning leaves. This package owns\n49|//     the reducer-level pair projections those transactions must\n50|//     carry (bundle, plugin resume, resumed/fork, finalize, bridge)\n51|//     and the checks that refuse a divergent pair with\n52|//     integrity_failure.\n53|//\n54|// Confirmation is a publication rule, not derivation input: the\n55|// set-profile transaction refuses an unconfirmed change to yolo, and\n56|// every chained profile.changed event is then authoritative by\n57|// construction — matching the sessquery admission, which reads only\n58|// the target. There is no time-expiring ownership lease in the\n59|// pinned Section 5.3, so \"losing or expired\" at set-profile means\n60|// the acting lease no longer equals the chain-head lease (a stale\n61|// epoch or a divergent same-epoch token); wall-clock liveness is not\n62|// authority.\n63|//\n64|// Stated bounds (not silent gaps):\n65|//\n66|//   - No named profile registry exists in the pinned specification:\n67|//     the profile vocabulary is exactly the standard|yolo enum named\n68|//     by the CLI and bridge flags. Absent-flag defaulting for ax\n69|//     start --profile belongs to the CLI-surface leaf, which passes\n70|//     this package an explicit value; ResolveCreationProfile refuses\n71|//     anything else, including empty.\n72|//   - No ax command, doctor result, or runtime capability claim is\n73|//     added. The set-profile transaction mints and appends the event\n74|//     the ax session set-profile surface will drive; CLI parsing,\n75|//     rendering, and the cliresult body stay with their owners.\n76|//   - On an eventless chain the acting lease opens sequence 1: the\n77|//     Lease Record binding of that opening lease belongs to the\n78|//     ownership-leases story, and the caller passes the winning\n79|//     lease. On a non-empty chain the acting lease must equal the\n80|//     chain head exactly; a greater-epoch acting lease is refused\n81|//     because set-profile authors under the current lease only —\n82|//     lease succession arrives through takeover flows, never through\n83|//     a profile event.\n84|//   - Set-profile replay recognizes an already-committed change by\n85|//     its request envelope (from, to, lease, author, instant) on the\n86|//     newest authoritative change. A retry under a superseded lease\n87|//     still refuses the lease first: replay never bypasses fencing.\n88|package sessprofile","final_result":true}}}
