{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000cb5d","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ae11-04bd-7bb0-aac5-3ecca198188f"},"sequence":1033,"recorded_at":1780531400002061,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"a44b1373-1c97-4578-936f-97327477c22e","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"a44b1373-1c97-4578-936f-97327477c22e","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"a44b1373-1c97-4578-936f-97327477c22e"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0ae17-ec2c-73b0-b719-9dd2e008d253"},"task_id":"01a0ae17-ec2c-73b0-b719-9dd2e008d253","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0ae17-ec2c-73b0-b719-9dd2e008d253","chunk":"edited\nchanged lines: lines 35-52\n--- original\n+++ updated\n@@\n-    {\n-        \"name\": \"R-closure-profile-changed\",\n-        \"file\": \"internal/sessprofile/profile.go\",\n-        \"old\": \"if closure != nil && !closure[event.ID] {\",\n-        \"new\": 'if closure != nil && !closure[event.ID] && event.Type != \"profile.changed\" {',\n-        \"bound\": \"Admit exactly profile.changed events outside the checkpoint closure; every other non-closure event stays excluded.\",\n-        \"cmd\": [\"go\", \"test\", \"./internal/sessprofile\", \"-run\",\n-                r\"^TestDeriveForHeadsExcludesLaterChange$\", \"-count=1\", \"-v\"],\n-    },\n-    {\n-        \"name\": \"R-compare-lease-lte\",\n-        \"file\": \"internal/sessprofile/profile.go\",\n-        \"old\": \"if a.Epoch < b.Epoch {\",\n-        \"new\": \"if a.Epoch <= b.Epoch {\",\n-        \"bound\": \"Collapse the equal-epoch order so the winning-lease equality arm is unreachable: same-lease chains refuse stale. Strengthening attack on an unmutated arm; happy-path derivation must go RED.\",\n-        \"cmd\": [\"go\", \"test\", \"./internal/sessprofile\", \"-run\",\n-                r\"^TestDeriveNewestChangeWins$\", \"-count=1\", \"-v\"],\n-    },\n+    {\n+        \"name\": \"R-closure-limit-plus-one\",\n+        \"file\": \"internal/sessprofile/profile.go\",\n+        \"old\": \"limit = position[id] + 1\",\n+        \"new\": \"limit = position[id] + 2\",\n+        \"bound\": \"Widen the checkpoint closure validation limit by exactly one event: the single post-closure corrupt event enters validation and checkChain refuses its repeated sequence, so DeriveForHeads errors where it must succeed.\",\n+        \"cmd\": [\"go\", \"test\", \"./internal/sessprofile\", \"-run\",\n+                r\"^TestDeriveForHeadsIgnoresPostClosureCorruption$\",\n+                \"-count=1\", \"-v\"],\n+    },\n+    {\n+        \"name\": \"R-first-seq-admits-2\",\n+        \"file\": \"internal/sessprofile/profile.go\",\n+        \"old\": (\"if event.Sequence != 1 {\\n\"\n+                '\\t\\t\\treturn nil, refuse(ErrInvalidTransition, \"first event %s must open its lease at sequence 1\", event.ID)'),\n+        \"new\": (\"if event.Sequence != 1 && event.Sequence != 2 {\\n\"\n+                '\\t\\t\\treturn nil, refuse(ErrInvalidTransition, \"first event %s must open its lease at sequence 1\", event.ID)'),\n+        \"bound\": \"Admit exactly the sequence-2 lease opener past the first-event gate (an arm the producer battery never mutated); the sequence-is-not-1 refusal disappears. NOTE: the brief-suggested compareLease '<=' variant is vacuous here: it sits inside an outer 'a.Epoch != b.Epoch' guard, so '<=' is behavior-identical to '<' and correctly SURVIVES; this plant attacks the order gate observably instead.\",\n+        \"cmd\": [\"go\", \"test\", \"./internal/sessprofile\", \"-run\",\n+                r\"^TestDeriveRefusesFirstEventViolations$\", \"-count=1\", \"-v\"],\n+    },\n","final_result":true}}}
